 if you  remember that it went well into move get  70 and that was actual game that Magnus  Carlsen made a huge mistake could have  actually won that game ended up a  drawing as he was not able to convert a  passed pawn that he probably should have  pretty distraught after that game but  this one decided okay  can't pull a fast one over on my  opponent so decides to go instead play  rook back here to eat one kind of the  normal move that you see in this opening  recover te8 cardiac and playing strong  defense but says hey let's let's  exchange material if you want I know  that you have kind of the advantage with  the white pieces in the last game so I'm  going to do everything I can to draw  this game or see if you can make a  mistake like you did earlier in the  tournament Bishop to f4 from Magnus  Carlsen just developing that dark square  Bishop rook takes Queen takes and then  out Knight back here to e8 me he kind of  had the decision here this Knight is  being attacked on d6 he's going to be  recapturing with this pawn more than  likely so he could either take here on  d4 trying to hold on to this material  and just give up double pawns on the  deef also after the pot or the bishop  takes pawn recaptures not up here to see  three more than likely not going to take  with his bishop here I'll say [ __ ]  you're back here to e5 or work here to  d1 attacking the pawn may be pawn up  here to f4 can't really take it because  then Queen up here to e4 attacking both  the bishop and the rook so if the bishop  comes back then this pawn is going to  fall although it's going to be difficult  to hold on to that material on board  this I just go and play Knight back here  to e8  not very aggressive but also just  playing somewhat defensive in this  position pawn here to c3 pawn to d5 so  just pushing his material up and getting  it opportunity for the light rare bishop  to get involved into the game Bishop to  d3 a pawn to g6 not over here to a 3 and  then pawn to c6 and this was where I  kind of saw the writing on the wall of  completely symmetrical both sides I  didn't really feel like karyakin was  going to be doing anything too crazy  because he could have from here plate  you know pawn to a5 he could have not  worried about this plate Knight to g7  and then tried to break things up on the  Queen side the board with his pawns but  karyakin like he's done so far in the  tournament said yeah I'm I'm fine with a  drawl I'll play as defensive as I need  to nothing's going to get past me on  this game and madness Karl  didn't seem to be okay with that as well  night over here to c29 to g7 Queen here  to d2 and then after Bishop to f5 there  was just a fury of exchanges on board  the Bishop takes Knight takes Knight  over here to e3 and they just started  exchanging material off the board and  Kuryakin said about Queen to e7 a do you  want to go and exchange Queens off the  board and Magnus Carlsen said yes I do  [ __ ] you're back here takes on e7 work  over here to e1 after the bishop comes  back a king here to f1 they push their  pawns up a little bit but then after  rook here to e8 the row comes up in  exchange and then both sides pretty much  said okay we have a bishop on board a  same color it's not an open board state  so the Bishop's going to be are going to  be doing too much we've only exchanged  one pawn off the war but there's no  material to even do too much so this was  after move 26 they do have to get to  move 34 to be a draw so they play the  rest of moves out in about a minute and  a half and then after that they decided  to after move 30 the bare minimum to go  ahead and announce a draw very  disappointing in my opinion the game  lasted about 35 minutes I actually got  to to the coverage about 28 minutes in  and then it was just rapid fire that  they were already playing rapid in blitz  tile chess  it didn't seem like either player wanted  to really be playing this particular  game Magnus Carlsen afterwards kind of  alluded that he apologized people that  said hey sorry you were hoping for  fireworks that was not my game plan  coming in cardiac and even kind of  jabbed at him a little bit which I  thought was interesting said you know  Magnus Carlsen he just wanted to trade  off pieces he didn't try to put me any  difficult spots which I thought was  weird since he had the white pieces but  hey if that's what he wanted to do  that's fine now Magnus Carlsen for his  credit he is the rapid chess champion  the last two years in a row and if  you're not kind of familiar with the  tiber because we will be taking a day  off and then coming back for a rapid and  blitz style tiebreaker so the first one  is rapid chess they'll be playing a  four-game series they both have 25  it's an in with each move they do get 10  seconds so different than the hundred  minutes they get now with a 30-second  much faster if for some reason it's  still tied after that they will play  blitz chess it will be a five-game  series and they'll have five minutes  with three seconds so very very quick  and then if no one's one after that then  they will play Armageddon which is a  horrible way to decide a victor but and  that whites actually given five minutes  blacks given four minutes and if it's a  tie then black wins because he had less  time that would be the weirdest way to  have a champion but it possibly could  happen now as we said Magnus Carlsen  feels really good about his chances with  a rapid chess so I'll hope it I hope it  works out if it doesn't I do think he's  going to look back on this game 12 and  say I pretty much didn't even try to win  this one so for everyone out there kind  of hoping for exciting game 12 you were  surely disappointed if there's players  out there that we're kind of excited for  more chess you are ecstatic because we  get at least four more games  assuming Madison doesn't win I'll take  three of those right away and then we  don't play that fourth one but all in  all we are going to get some extra chess  so I thank you guys for watching short  video you probably could even tell from  the length of this video that it was  going to be a fast one the other games  may be as fast as well hopefully we'll  have some crazy exchange with a fast  checkmate that always be exciting but  thanks for watching I'll see you in the  rapid chess in two days bye

